ProjectAnalyticDescription=Project analytic expenses, never posted to accountancy
ProjectAnalyticDescriptionLong=Lets you allocate a cost to a project for the project Overview (Profit) tab, without ever impacting accountancy (purchases journal, FEC/ledger export). Useful for a cost already booked globally elsewhere (e.g. bulk purchase of consumables) whose share you want to track against a specific project.
ProjectAnalyticExpense=Project analytic expense
ProjectAnalyticExpenses=Project analytic expenses
NewProjectAnalyticExpense=New project analytic expense
AddProjectAnalyticExpense=Add analytic expense
ListProjectAnalyticExpenseAssociatedProject=Analytic expenses (not posted to accountancy)
RealSupplier=Real supplier (informative)
ProjectAnalyticExpenseRealSupplierHelp=Real supplier of the expense, for information only. Never used by accountancy.
ProjectAnalyticExpenseSourceInvoice=Source supplier invoice (traceability)
ProjectAnalyticExpenseSourceInvoiceHelp=Global supplier invoice where this cost was already booked (e.g. bulk purchase of consumables). This link is purely informative: it lets you trace back the origin of the amount, but has no impact on accountancy. This analytic expense is never exported to accountancy (purchases journal, FEC): it only feeds the project Profit calculation, so it never duplicates the cost already booked globally on the supplier invoice.
